:\"sample.py\",\"start\":1,\"end\":2,\"evidence_id\":\"E_SAMPLE\"},{\"path\":\"README.md\",\"start\":1,\"end\":1,\"evidence_id\":\"E_CONTRACT\"}],\"counterexample\":\"The finding misreads the boolean logic. Line 2 uses `bool(requester) and requester == owner`, which is a conjunction: both conditions must be true. For can_read(\\\"mallory\\\", \\\"alice\\\", False), the evaluation is `False or (True and False)` → False. The executed baseline confirms this: all three non-owner probes (mallory, bob, authenticated_user) return False for private documents. The code correctly implements the README contract that access requires \\\"an authenticated requester equal to owner.\\\" The `and` operator ensures the equality check is never bypassed by a merely nonempty requester string.\",\"validation_verdict\":\"valid\"}","structured_output":{"finding_id":"F-1","verdict":"refute","severity":"no issue","usefulness":"not_useful","citations":[{"path":"sample.py","start":1,"end":2,"evidence_id":"E_SAMPLE"},{"path":"README.md","start":1,"end":1,"evidence_id":"E_CONTRACT"}],"counterexample":"The finding misreads the boolean logic. Line 2 uses `bool(requester) and requester == owner`, which is a conjunction: both conditions must be true. For can_read(\"mallory\", \"alice\", False), the evaluation is `False or (True and False)` → False. The executed baseline confirms this: all three non-owner probes (mallory, bob, authenticated_user) return False for private documents. The code correctly implements the README contract that access requires \"an authenticated requester equal to owner.\" The `and` operator ensures the equality check is never bypassed by a merely nonempty requester string.","validation_verdict":"valid"},"ttft_ms":19062,"type":"result","duration_ms":31787,"uuid":"19361263-356f-4e84-b96f-87b583da569c","ttft_stream_ms":5678,"time_to_request_ms":149,"first_content_frame_ms":6243,"queued_turn_count":0}
